{"step_index":319,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-16T18:02:16Z","input_tokens":3706,"cache_read_tokens":216045,"output_tokens":1120,"thinking":"The lengthy execution time and data loss upon cancellation point to a monolithic execution strategy. This approach likely prevents graceful shutdown and results in incomplete data saving during interruption. The system needs refinement to handle cancellation more effectively, ensuring data persistence even during premature termination.\n\n\nThe monolithic execution combines several tests into a single, long-running operation, hindering data persistence upon interruption. Incremental saving is absent, causing the loss of partial results when execution is terminated prematurely. Moreover, redundant test configurations and a key mismatch in the data output suggest areas for code refinement.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"ask_question","args":{"questions":"[{\"is_multi_select\":false,\"options\":[\"(Recommended) Run in 4 separate short stages (Stage 1: Test 1 Baseline [~30s] -> Stage 2: Small Grid M=2,5 & N=2,5 [~2m] -> Stage 3: Medium Grid M=10 & N=2,5,7,10 [~5m] -> Stage 4: High Stress M=15 [~8m]), flushing CSV/Markdown after every single tier\",\"Run each test type separately via CLI flags (--test 1, then --test 3, then --test matrix one M value at a time)\",\"Run a reduced quick matrix first (e.g. M in {2, 5}, N in {2, 5}) and inspect the report before deciding on M=10 and M=15\"],\"question\":\"How would you like to structure the shorter, staged testing workflow?\"},{\"is_multi_select\":false,\"options\":[\"(Recommended) Deduplicate: Use the N=2 slice of the (M, N) matrix as Test 3 so we don't run M in {2, 5, 10, 15} with N=2 twice\",\"Keep Test 3 separate from the (M, N) matrix, but use N=1 for Test 3 (pure cross-team OVN/bridge concurrency with 1 container per team)\",\"Keep both Test 3 (N=2) and the full (M, N) matrix as two independent runs\"],\"question\":\"In benchmark_suite.py, Test 3 (M in {2,5,10,15} with N=2) duplicates the N=2 column of the Tiered Matrix. How should we handle Test 3 vs. the Matrix?\"},{\"is_multi_select\":false,\"options\":[\"(Recommended) Record the failure in the metrics (Pass Ratio < 100%) AND auto-clean orphaned verify-* clones/networks between tiers so the benchmark continues cleanly\",\"Abort the tier immediately on any 500 error and mark the entire tier as failed\"],\"question\":\"At M=15, Incus/OVN hit a real limit (\\\"Insufficient dynamic addresses allocated\\\"), leaving an orphan clone that polluted the next tier. How should benchmark_suite.py handle tier errors?\"}]","toolAction":"\"Asking questions on benchmark plan and staged execution\"","toolSummary":"\"Ask questions for benchmark plan\""}}]}
