{"step_index":325,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-16T18:10:49Z","input_tokens":2130,"cache_read_tokens":224625,"output_tokens":14542,"thinking":"User requires a comprehensive, plot-ready CSV export of all substage timings from testing for thesis data analysis. This necessitates careful CSV design to include all relevant time data points with appropriate headers for direct plotting in common tools. The goal is to ensure the CSV structure is directly usable without pre-processing for plotting and analysis.\n\n\nInitial CSV design prioritizes two files for maximum plotting flexibility. The first, `thesis_summary_results.csv`, will aggregate performance statistics for each test scenario. This file will include metadata and all time data points for provisioning and deployment sub-stages. A second file is likely also needed to support micro-phase level data from the Deployment sub-stage.\n\n\n`thesis_summary_results.csv` must include all deployment sub-stage timing metrics, focusing on average, p50, and p95 percentiles for creation, pushing, starting, runtime network, and database recording. Also include the total standard deviation of deployment time.\n\nFor sub-stage 3 (OVN sandbox verification), extract and include all macro and micro-phase verification timings such as total wall time, average total time, and percentile values, along with setup, OVN network creation, CoW clone, and clone connection times. These will form the second CSV file.\n\n\nThe second CSV file, `thesis_raw_samples.csv`, will require a unique row for each team's execution within each tier and cycle. This granular data structure enables detailed visualizations like boxplots, violin plots, and CDFs. Key verification substage metrics, including clone start, clone runtime, runner execution, readiness checks, command execution, and cleanup times (average, p50, and p95), will be included.\n\nTeardown substage timings, such as wall time, machine teardown, team teardown, and individual team teardown metrics (average, p95), will be incorporated into the raw sample data. RAM usage metrics—baseline, after deployment, after verification, and after teardown—are critical for understanding resource consumption and will also be tracked within the raw data.\n\n\nRaw sample data CSV structure confirmed. Identified required columns for per-team timings and test metadata. Deployment and verification sub-stage timings are included. Need to confirm and incorporate individual container-level timings from the responses.\n\n\nConsidering that detailed container-level timings are available, the CSV structure should be expanded. Plan to generate a tier-level summary, a raw team samples CSV, a Markdown report, and a JSON state file. The summaries will now include the per-container timing data and RAM usage.\n\nDecided to construct the updated benchmark script locally, copy it to the remote server, and then show the user the anticipated CSV column structure. The detailed CSV column structures will be displayed to the user.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"Append":"false","CodeContent":"\"import argparse\\nimport asyncio\\nimport csv\\nimport json\\nimport logging\\nimport math\\nimport os\\nimport sys\\nimport time\\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, List, Optional, Tuple\\n\\n# Ensure blueagent and tests are importable\\nsys.path.insert(0, '/home/debian/bluectfd/blueagent/src')\\nsys.path.insert(0, '/home/debian/bluectfd/blueagent')\\nos.environ['BLUEAGENT_CTFD_API_TOKEN'] = 'secret-token'\\n\\nfrom blueagent.engine.incus import IncusEngine\\nfrom tests.usability.client import BlueAgentTestClient\\n\\nlogging.basicConfig(\\n    level=logging.INFO,\\n    format='%(asctime)s [%(levelname)s] %(message)s',\\n    datefmt='%H:%M:%S'\\n)\\nlogger = logging.getLogger('benchmark')\\n\\nSTATE_JSON_PATH = '/home/debian/bluectfd/blueagent/tests/thesis_stress_test_state.json'\\nCSV_SUMMARY_PATH = '/home/debian/bluectfd/blueagent/tests/thesis_stress_test_results.csv'\\nCSV_RAW_SAMPLES_PATH = '/home/debian/bluectfd/blueagent/tests/thesis_raw_team_samples.csv'\\nREPORT_OUTPUT_PATH = '/home/debian/bluectfd/blueagent/tests/thesis_stress_test_report.md'\\n\\n\\ndef percentile(data: List[float], p: float) -> float:\\n    if not data:\\n        return 0.0\\n    sorted_data = sorted(data)\\n    k = (len(sorted_data) - 1) * (p / 100.0)\\n    f = math.floor(k)\\n    c = math.ceil(k)\\n    if f == c:\\n        return round(sorted_data[int(k)], 4)\\n    d0 = sorted_data[int(f)] * (c - k)\\n    d1 = sorted_data[int(c)] * (k - f)\\n    return round(d0 + d1, 4)\\n\\n\\ndef calculate_stats(values: List[float]) -> Dict[str, float]:\\n    if not values:\\n        return {'avg': 0.0, 'p50': 0.0, 'p95': 0.0, 'min': 0.0, 'max': 0.0, 'std': 0.0}\\n    avg = sum(values) / len(values)\\n    variance = sum((x - avg) ** 2 for x in values) / len(values)\\n    return {\\n        'avg': round(avg, 4),\\n        'p50': percentile(values, 50),\\n        'p95': percentile(values, 95),\\n        'min': round(min(values), 4),\\n        'max': round(max(values), 4),\\n        'std': round(math.sqrt(variance), 4),\\n    }\\n\\n\\ndef get_sys\n<truncated 39169 bytes>","Description":"\"Refactored benchmark_suite.py with full sub-stage and micro-phase CSV exports, incremental checkpointing, and parallel orphan cleanup\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"/home/davidel/.gemini/antigravity/brain/335ea41a-df46-4ffa-bb4c-eefc5a5248cd/scratch/benchmark_suite.py\"","toolAction":"\"Updating benchmark_suite.py with full sub-stage CSV exports\"","toolSummary":"\"Write updated benchmark_suite.py\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
